use core
use web/server
use web/script
use def/site.page
use components/nav
use components/home
use components/hello
use components/bmi
use components/missing
use def/routes

// run with:  def-lang run website   then open http://localhost:8000
// settings.toml says how it runs (port, watching changed files); save it to change them while it runs.
//
// A single page application: the page (def/site.page.def) holds the components, with
// the script that switches between them without reloading. A component is one file
// with its view (HTML), its style (CSS), its script (JavaScript) and the defs that
// work out its data; def/routes.def says at which address each is sent.
//
//   def/site.page.def        the one page the components live in
//   components/nav.def       the links at the top
//   components/*.def         one file per component: home, hello, bmi, missing
//   def/routes.def           every address the website answers
//   settings.toml            port, everyone, watch
//
// The web server and the script come from the web library (web/server and
// web/script), installed with def-lang install.

start the server
